      "rerank_score_norm": 0.8238128708064788,
      "final_score": 0.5502755359715883,
      "text": "Details of the quality of included studies were shown in Fig. 2. Randomization was performed in all studies, but only 4 studies reported the details of random sequence generation. [40,45,47,48] Only 1 study [45] reported the information of allocation concealment, and none of the other studies mentioned it. Some included studies were assessed as having high risks cause because they did not describe the blinding process. One study reported that the outcome assessment was blinded. [45] Incomplete outcome data were reported in 7 trails, and 8 trails conducted selective reporting with a low risk of bias. Five trials reported other kinds of bias. [39,42,43,45,48] In general, the overall risk of bias in included studies is pretty high.",
